  "reason": "The strongest evidence is that scvi_n200 + ImageNet ViT-L multimodal models are far better than scgpt-based ones, with the best result at 0.725 using multiprofile, transformer aggregation, and weighted fusion. However, all completed experiments are multiprofile, so the effect of profile setting is an important unresolved uncertainty. config_039 tests whether the same strong RNA and image encoders with weighted fusion can match or beat the multiprofile model in a singleprofile setting, clarifying whether multiprofile aggregation is adding useful signal or unnecessary cost/complexity. This is a good use of experiment 9 because it exploits the best-known encoders while probing a major untested design choice before the final experiment. Expected cost is moderate and likely lower than the multiprofile transformer weighted model because it avoids multiprofile aggregation, though it remains nontrivial due to the ViT-L image encoder, roughly comparable to or slightly below config_024's 3.60 GPU hours."
}

